use Libraries.Web.Page.QuorumPage

/*
    Complete Quest Behaviors.
    Converted from the old Lesson page by plan 13's generator: the same
    words, now without Tailwind.
*/
class CompleteQuest is QuorumPage

    on create
        SetLocation("lessons/Scenes/quests.html")
        // The name lists and links use, and the series and track it belongs
        // to: its section and picture.
        SetShortTitle("Complete our Quest")
        SetSectionName("Experience Programming in Quorum (EPIQ)")
        // For search engines and link previews, and what lists of pages say.
        SetDescription("Complete our Quest at Experience Programming in Quorum (EPIQ).")
        SetSummary(" completing our quest.")
    end

    action Setup
        SetWebPageTitle("Complete Quest Behaviors - Quorum Programming Language")
        Title("Complete Quest Behaviors")
        Paragraph("Complete your game and add Accessibility features")
        LearningObjectives()
        BrainstormAccessibility15Minutes()
        BuildAccessibilityFeatures35Minutes()
        Captioning10Minutes()
    end

    private action LearningObjectives
        Section("Learning Objectives")
        Paragraph("In this final session, we have one task left: finish our game. Our goal is to brainstorm about accessibility features, including spatialized sound, and think about what would make our game more accessible broadly.")
        Paragraph("You will:")
        BulletList()
        ListItem("Learn about Accessibility")
        ListItem("Learn about Spatialized Audio")
        ListItem("Practice coding")
    end

    private action BrainstormAccessibility15Minutes
        Section("Brainstorm Accessibility (15 minutes)")
        Paragraph("Whenever we invent something, it is important to find a balance in our brainstorming. We want to think big about what would solve our user's problems, but we also want to be practical so that we can engineer our idea in a reasonable amount of time. For this part of the session, we will brainstorm with our group for 10 minutes on the features we think we could add to our game to make it more accessible. In the next part, we will try to build at least one of them.")
    end

    private action BuildAccessibilityFeatures35Minutes
        Section("Build Accessibility Features (35 Minutes)")
        Paragraph("While any accessibility feature could be chosen, consider looking at spatialized sound because coding it is straightforward. Notably, you might consider writing code that changes the audio channel depending on the direction of an item or you could use spatialized sound to provide more information about the environment in general. Other accessibility features that could be built include using sounds to indicate if a character bumped into a wall or really anything. The point is to be creative and think about the following question: what would make this game more accessible, to whom, and how do we invent that?")
    end

    private action Captioning10Minutes
        Section("Captioning (10 minutes)")
        Paragraph("Voice overs and spatialized sounds are neat for computer games. They can be used both to create a narrative that has real actors telling a player what to do and to provide a level of context and immersion. However, sound has a downside in that it is not accessible to people that are deaf or hard of hearing. One way we can add support for our game is to make it have closed or open captions. Investigate the "):Link("Label", "/Libraries/Game/Graphics/Label.html"):Text(" class in Quorum and speculate on how we could use it to add captions to our game.")
    end
end
